+    The keyword-only *default_factory* constructs a fallback lazily. When
+    provided, it is called without arguments exactly once on empty input,
+    and its result is returned unchanged. It is never called on nonempty
+    input. ``None`` means no factory.
+
+    Providing both *default* (including ``None``) and a non-``None``
+    *default_factory* raises ``ValueError``. Otherwise, a non-``None`` factory
+    must be callable or ``TypeError`` is raised. These options are validated
+    before consuming *iterable*. Source and factory exceptions propagate.
+
+    If neither *default* nor a factory is provided and there are no items
